The MIT licence in LICENSE covers this repository's source code only. It does
not cover the binary assets in assets/, which come from elsewhere and carry
their own terms.

Each asset is listed below with its licence, the credit that licence requires,
and what was changed from the original. **If you ship a build that contains one
of these files, its credit has to travel with it** — including into bundled or
minified output, where it is easy to lose by accident.

One entry per asset. Add to this file whenever an asset is added; see
"Adding an asset" at the end.


